  "notes": "B.S. in Marketing, College of Business (AACSB-accredited). SEMESTER SYSTEM — all credits are semester hours. Built from the official MSU Denver 2024-2025 Undergraduate Catalog program page for Marketing Major, B.S. (https://msudenver.catalog.acalog.com/preview_program.php?catoid=48&poid=11836) for the major requirements, and the official BSBA Planning Guide & Checklist (https://www.msudenver.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/BSBA-Planning-Guide_Checklist-23-24.pdf) for the shared College of Business core structure. Structure: General Studies 34cr (ENG 1010/1020, COMM 1010/1100, MTH 1310, Arts & Humanities 6cr, Historical 3cr, Natural & Physical Sciences 6cr, ECO 2010/2020 for Social & Behavioral Sciences), Business Core 36cr (BUS 1850/1950, ACC 2010/2020, CIS 2010/3300/3320, FIN 3300, MGT 2210/3000, MKT 3000, MGT 4950 Senior Experience), Additional College of Business 6cr (MTH 1320, BUS 3040), Marketing Major 24cr (MKT 3310 Consumer Behavior, MKT 3010 Marketing Research, MKT 3710 International Marketing, MKT 4560 Marketing Strategy, + 12cr upper-division MKT electives), General Electives 20cr. C- or better required in each major course; 2.0 average required in the Business Core; C- or better required in MGT 4950. 120 semester credits total.",
